Bound the accepted-token-derived block-table columns to the requesting row.

In align mode the source column is computed from the accepted-token count,
which can put it before the start or past the end of this request's row in the
block table. Mask the read against the row width instead, so an out-of-range
column yields nothing rather than another request's block.

